  "description": "Moderation rollbacks (ADR 0024): a `restore` entry sets each listed cell, [index, cell byte, ...shield layer expiry times], to its value, takes no time and changes counters like the ops do. It puts a hammered cell of an O brick back with the links into it, then is refused (changing nothing) for: emptying a cell that neighbours link into; each check alone on the isolated cell (12, 12) = 204: an empty cell with bits, an empty cell with a layer, more layers than maxShield, a byte over 255, a repeated index, a link to another colour, a link right off the map's edge (x = 15, which would wrap onto (0, 13)), and, after a valid linked pair there, emptying the cell its left neighbour links into (the pair is then removed again); a layer at or before the clock (2000), a layer outliving one placed now (after clock + lifetime, 12000), and unsorted indices. A restore adds a layer (expiring at 9000) to the restored cell, then one empties an I brick so an O brick fits in its place. Later hammers break the restored layer, clear the restored cell, and clear (2, 2) once its own layer expired at 11000.",
